1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,411
我们在一些模拟的玩具数据上跑了
We ran the MMD metric from Josh's package on some toy cells,

2
00:00:04,411 --> 00:00:06,885
包里的 MMD 指标，它给出 0.326
and it said zero point three two six.

3
00:00:07,205 --> 00:00:08,317
这个数对吗？
Is that right?

4
00:00:08,367 --> 00:00:12,428
光看是看不出来的，没有人能用肉眼检查这种数字
You can't tell by looking. Nobody can check a number like that by eye.

5
00:00:12,428 --> 00:00:16,431
但你可以在答案已知的数据上检查一个指标
But you can check a metric on data where you already know the answer.

6
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:19,971
测试就是这么回事：一个答案已知的问题
That's all a test is: a question with a known answer,

7
00:00:19,971 --> 00:00:23,405
由你的代码自己作答，你每问一次它就答一次
which your code answers by itself, every time you ask.

8
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:29,927
Josh 已经写了一个，在 test_evaluation.py 里
Josh already wrote one, in test_evaluation.py.

9
00:00:30,247 --> 00:00:32,047
三个细胞，两个基因
Three cells, two genes.

10
00:00:32,167 --> 00:00:34,791
预测和真实值是同一团点
The prediction and the truth are the same cloud.

11
00:00:34,967 --> 00:00:40,317
MMD 用核函数比较两团点：把两团各自内部的平均相似度相加
MMD compares two clouds with a kernel. Add the average similarity inside each cloud,

12
00:00:40,317 --> 00:00:43,820
再减去两团之间平均相似度的两倍
then subtract twice the average similarity across them.

13
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:49,504
当两团点完全相同时，这三个平均值都相等，所以答案一定是零
When the clouds are identical, all three averages are equal, so the answer must be zero.

14
00:00:49,667 --> 00:00:54,857
最后一行写的正是这一点：断言（assert）分数约等于零
The last line says exactly that: assert that the score is approximately zero.

15
00:00:54,857 --> 00:01:00,115
之所以是「约等于」，是因为浮点数加加减减，很少恰好等于零
Approximately, because sums of floating-point numbers are rarely exactly zero.

16
00:01:00,115 --> 00:01:01,867
如果是，测试就悄悄通过
If it is, the test passes,

17
00:01:01,867 --> 00:01:05,709
如果不是，它会醒目地报错失败，并给出两个数
silently. If not, it fails, loudly, showing both numbers.

18
00:01:09,633 --> 00:01:12,815
你从不需要自己调用测试，只要输入 pytest
You never call a test yourself. You type pytest.

19
00:01:12,815 --> 00:01:15,930
它会找到名字以 test_ 开头的文件
It finds files named test underscore something,

20
00:01:15,930 --> 00:01:20,769
运行其中名字以 test 开头的每个函数，并逐一报告结果
runs every function whose name starts with test, and reports on each one.

21
00:01:20,933 --> 00:01:24,919
单独运行时，Josh 的 MMD 测试不到两秒就通过了
On its own, Josh's MMD test passes in under two seconds,

22
00:01:24,919 --> 00:01:28,122
而且大部分时间只是在导入库
and most of that is just importing libraries.

23
00:01:28,442 --> 00:01:31,898
停下来猜一猜：对整个文件夹运行，会发生什么？
Pause and predict: what happens when you run the whole folder?

24
00:01:36,066 --> 00:01:40,623
它会提前停下。 test_model.py 不是测试函数，而是一个脚本
It stops early. test_model.py isn't a test function, it's a script.

25
00:01:40,623 --> 00:01:43,548
pytest 一导入它，里面的代码就开始执行
Its code runs the moment pytest imports it.

26
00:01:43,548 --> 00:01:48,173
在集群外，它找不到配置文件；在集群上更糟
Off the cluster it can't find its config. On the cluster it's worse:

27
00:01:48,173 --> 00:01:54,498
它先加载好几个 GB 的图谱文件，再在 setup 里崩溃，一个测试都还没跑
it loads the multi-gigabyte atlas files, then crashes in setup, before a single test has run.

28
00:01:54,666 --> 00:01:57,082
好的测试只靠你的代码就能跑
A good test runs on your code alone.

29
00:01:57,082 --> 00:01:59,632
不需要集群、不需要几个 GB 的文件、不需要 GPU
No cluster, no gigabyte files, no GPU.

30
00:01:59,632 --> 00:02:03,456
正因为如此，它才快到可以在每次修改后都跑一遍
That's what makes it fast enough to run after every edit.

31
00:02:08,333 --> 00:02:12,305
已知答案从哪里来？ 从指标的含义来
Where do known answers come from? From what the metric means.

32
00:02:12,305 --> 00:02:17,122
停下来猜一猜：把一团点推离另一团，MMD 应该怎么变？
Pause and predict: push one cloud away from the other. What should MMD do?

33
00:02:21,300 --> 00:02:23,100
它应该变大，结果也确实如此
It should grow, and it does.

34
00:02:23,156 --> 00:02:26,826
我们测了一下：平移 0、0.5、1、2
We measured it: shift by nothing, half, one, then two,

35
00:02:26,826 --> 00:02:32,670
MMD 从 0 升到 0.08，再到 0.29，再到 0.85
and MMD climbs from zero, to point zero eight, to point two nine, to point eight five.

36
00:02:32,833 --> 00:02:36,502
完美的预测，R² 应该等于 1，结果确实如此
A perfect prediction should score an R squared of one, and it does.

37
00:02:36,822 --> 00:02:39,957
把预测的细胞顺序打乱，它就掉到几乎为零
Shuffle the predicted cells, and it drops to almost zero,

38
00:02:39,957 --> 00:02:43,457
因为这种 R² 是把预测的第 i 个细胞和真实的第 i 个细胞配对比较的
because this R squared pairs cell one with cell one.

39
00:02:43,777 --> 00:02:48,569
记住这一点。这每一句话都能变成一个五行左右的测试
Remember that. Each of those sentences becomes a test of about five lines.

40
00:02:48,889 --> 00:02:52,367
再注意一下数据：都是在测试内部造出来的小数组
And notice the data: tiny arrays built inside the test.

41
00:02:52,687 --> 00:02:55,609
测试检查的是逻辑，不是生物学
The test checks the logic, not the biology.

42
00:03:00,067 --> 00:03:02,755
现在来一个不只是检查算术的测试
Now a test that does more than check arithmetic.

43
00:03:03,075 --> 00:03:07,747
在真实实验里，小鼠和人类的测试集细胞数不一样
In a real experiment, the mouse and human test sets have different numbers of cells.

44
00:03:08,067 --> 00:03:11,736
停下来猜一猜：R2Evaluation 能接受这种情况吗？
Pause and predict: does R2Evaluation accept that?

45
00:03:15,900 --> 00:03:20,447
不能。 我们试了 5 个小鼠细胞对 7 个人类细胞
It doesn't. We tried five mouse cells against seven human cells,

46
00:03:20,447 --> 00:03:25,421
它在第 313 行崩溃了：5 行没法和 7 行对齐
and it crashed at line 313. Five rows can't be lined up against seven.

47
00:03:25,421 --> 00:03:29,116
而如果是 5 对 5，它根本不会崩溃
And with five against five, it doesn't crash at all:

48
00:03:29,116 --> 00:03:34,375
它会把毫不相关的细胞配成对，然后报出 R² 0.103
it pairs unrelated cells and reports an R squared of point one zero three.

49
00:03:34,534 --> 00:03:36,390
原因在它的公式里
The reason is in its formula.

50
00:03:36,710 --> 00:03:40,822
它和你重建脚本里的逐基因 R² 是同一个公式
It's the same per-gene R squared as in your reconstruction script,

51
00:03:40,822 --> 00:03:44,561
在那里每个细胞都有一个真正的搭档：它自己的重建结果
where every cell has a true partner: its own reconstruction.

52
00:03:44,881 --> 00:03:50,470
而你的基准用的是另一种 R²：比较每个基因的平均表达
Your benchmark uses a different R squared: it compares the average expression of each gene.

53
00:03:50,790 --> 00:03:53,840
均值 R² 根本察觉不到打乱
An R squared of means wouldn't even notice a shuffle.

54
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,325
那么，实验需要的是哪一种？
So, which one does the experiment need?

55
00:03:56,645 --> 00:03:58,409
测试回答不了这个问题
The test can't answer that.

56
00:03:58,459 --> 00:04:02,875
它把一个隐藏的假设，变成了一个你现在可以有意识地做出的决定
It turned a hidden assumption into a decision you can now make on purpose.

57
00:04:08,333 --> 00:04:09,883
测试是分层的
Tests come in layers.

58
00:04:09,933 --> 00:04:14,264
最底层是单元测试：一个类、玩具数组、几毫秒
At the bottom are unit tests: one class, toy arrays, milliseconds.

59
00:04:14,584 --> 00:04:15,916
这种要多写
Write many of these.

60
00:04:15,966 --> 00:04:16,987
中间一层
In the middle,

61
00:04:16,987 --> 00:04:22,703
用一份 toy config 和几个很小的 h5ad 文件跑完整个 Experiment
the whole Experiment runs on a few tiny h5ad files, from a toy config. Seconds.

62
00:04:22,703 --> 00:04:24,203
几秒钟，写几个就够
A handful is enough.

63
00:04:24,203 --> 00:04:29,961
Josh 的 toy_config.yaml 更新之后，就是这一层的雏形
Josh's toy_config.yaml is the seed of this layer, once it's brought up to date.

64
00:04:30,133 --> 00:04:34,146
最上层是在真实图谱上运行的 e24_replica notebook
At the top is the e24_replica notebook on the real atlas:

65
00:04:34,146 --> 00:04:36,469
要几分钟到几小时，在集群上跑
minutes to hours, on the cluster.

66
00:04:36,789 --> 00:04:40,138
等下面几层都通过了再跑它，而不是用它来代替下面几层
Run it once the layers below are green, not instead of them.

67
00:04:40,300 --> 00:04:43,999
工作循环是：改一处，跑 pytest
The working loop: change one thing, run pytest, see green,

68
00:04:43,999 --> 00:04:46,422
看到全绿，然后才回到 notebook
and only then go back to the notebook.

69
00:04:50,267 --> 00:04:54,579
回顾一下。0.326 这个数没人能用肉眼检查
Recap. Nobody can check zero point three two six by eye,

70
00:04:54,579 --> 00:04:59,910
但你可以检查代码在该给 0、该给 1、该变大的地方，是否恰好如此
but you can check that the code gives zero, one, and more, exactly where it must.

71
00:05:00,230 --> 00:05:02,827
测试是一个答案已知的问题
A test is a question with a known answer,

72
00:05:02,827 --> 00:05:06,566
pytest 会运行每个名字以 test 开头的函数
and pytest runs every function whose name starts with test.

73
00:05:06,734 --> 00:05:10,604
已知答案来自指标的含义：相同的两团点给出 0
Known answers come from meaning: identical clouds give zero,

74
00:05:10,604 --> 00:05:14,926
完美预测给出 1，平移越大距离越大
a perfect prediction gives one, and more shift gives more distance.

75
00:05:15,246 --> 00:05:19,961
测试还能暴露一个假设：R2Evaluation 是按行配对的
A test can also expose an assumption: R2Evaluation pairs rows.

76
00:05:20,281 --> 00:05:23,672
另外，测试要分层：先跑单元测试，最后才跑 notebook
And test in layers: unit tests first, the notebook last.

77
00:05:23,834 --> 00:05:27,343
你的练习：把每个已知答案都写成一个测试
Your exercises: turn each known answer into a test,

78
00:05:27,343 --> 00:05:31,816
把 test_model 的代码挪进一个使用小文件的测试函数里
move test_model's code into a test function that uses tiny files,

79
00:05:31,816 --> 00:05:35,119
并决定实验指的是哪一种 R²
and decide which R squared the experiment means.
